er":"Frank Gehry","explanation":"Frank Gehry is associated with Guggenheim Museum Bilbao.","work":"Guggenheim Museum Bilbao","artist":"Frank Gehry","priority":5,"proof":"Guggenheim Museum Bilbao","format":"single_choice","kind":"source_pdf_association","sourceType":"reviewed_pdf"},{"id":"PDF34-Q-164-B","nodeId":"PDF34-FACT-164","source":"Important people from the past year papers By~Kaan Özhan.pdf","page":223,"group":"architecture-modern","major":"Architecture","era":"20th century","stem":"Which of these works or projects is associated with Frank Gehry?","choices":["Guggenheim Museum Bilbao","Villa Savoye in Poissy","Whitney Museum in New York","Ville Radieuse urban design","The Shard in London"],"answer":"Guggenheim Museum Bilbao","explanation":"Frank Gehry is associated with Guggenheim Museum Bilbao.","work":"Guggenheim Museum Bilbao","artist":"Frank Gehry","priority":5,"proof":"Guggenheim Museum Bilbao","format":"single_choice","kind":"source_pdf_reverse","sourceType":"reviewed_pdf"},{"id":"PDF34-Q-165-A","nodeId":"PDF34-FACT-165","source":"Important people from the past year papers By~Kaan Özhan.pdf","page":224,"group":"architecture-modern","major":"Architecture","era":"20th century","stem":"Which architect is associated with Dancing House in Prague?","choices":["Frank Gehry and Vlado Milunić","Le Corbusier and Pierre Jeanneret","Eugène Viollet-le-Duc","Pier Luigi Nervi","Frank Gehry"],"answer":"Frank Gehry and Vlado Milunić","explanation":"Frank Gehry and Vlado Milunić is associated with Dancing House in Prague.","work":"Dancing House in Prague","artist":"Frank Gehry and Vlado Milunić","priority":4,"proof":"Vlado Milunić","format":"single_choice","kind":"source_pdf_association","sourceType":"reviewed_pdf"},{"id":"PDF34-Q-165-B","nodeId":"PDF34-FACT-165","source":"Important people from the past year papers By~Kaan Özhan.pdf","page":224,"group":"architecture-modern","major":"Architecture","era":"20th century","stem":"Which of these works or projects is associated with Frank Gehry and Vlado Milunić?","choices":["Dancing House in Prague","engineering and architecture with reinforced concrete","Unity Temple","restoration of the medieval walls of Carcassonne","restoration of Notre-Dame de Paris"],"answer":"Dancing House in Prague","explanation":"Frank Gehry and Vlado Milunić is associated with Dancing House in Prague.","work":"Dancing House in Prague","artist":"Frank Gehry and Vlado Milunić","priority":4,"proof":"Vlado Milunić","format":"single_choice","kind":"source_pdf_reverse","sourceType":"reviewed_pdf"},{"id":"PDF34-Q-166-A","nodeId":"PDF34-FACT-166","source":"Important people from the past year papers By~Kaan Özhan.pdf","page":225,"group":"architecture-modern","major":"Architecture","era":"20th century","stem":"Which architect is associated with Guggenheim Abu Dhabi design?","choices":["Frank Gehry","Ludwig Mies van der Rohe","Frank Lloyd Wright","Renzo Piano","Pier Luigi Nervi"],"answer":"Frank Gehry","explanation":"Frank Gehry is associated with Guggenheim Abu Dhabi design.","work":"Guggenheim Abu Dhabi design","artist":"Frank Gehry","priority":3,"proof":"Architect Frank Gehry","format":"single_choice","kind":"source_pdf_association","sourceType":"reviewed_pdf"},{"id":"PDF34-Q-167-A","nodeId":"PDF34-FACT-167","source":"Important people from the past year papers By~Kaan Özhan.pdf","page":226,"group":"architecture-modern","major":"Architecture","era":"20th century","stem":"Which architect is associated with Jay Pritzker Pavilion in Chicago?","choices":["Frank Gehry","Pier Luigi Nervi","Walter Gropius","Le Corbusier","Ludwig Mies van der Rohe"],"answer":"Frank Gehry","explanation":"Frank Gehry is associated with Jay Pritzker Pavilion in Chicago.","work":"Jay Pritzker Pavilion in Chicago","artist":"Frank Gehry","priority":4,"proof":"Jay Pritzker Pavilion","format":"single_choice","kind":"source_pdf_association","sourceType":"reviewed_pdf"},{"id":"PDF34-CON-001-A","nodeId":"PDF34-CONFACT-001","source":"Important people from the past year papers By~Kaan Özhan.pdf","page":10,"group":"science","major":"Science & Tech","era":"Early modern","stem":"In Vitruvius's architectural triad, which Latin term means beauty?","choices":["venustas","firmitas","utilitas","gravitas","pietas"],"answer":"venustas","explanation":"Vitruvius used venustas for beauty; firmitas and utilitas refer to firmness and usefulness.","work":"Vitruvian design: beauty","artist":"venustas","priority":5,"proof":"venustas","format":"single_choice","kind":"source_pdf_context","sourceType":"reviewed_pdf"},{"id":"PDF34-CON-002-A","nodeId":"PDF34-CONFACT-002","source":"Important people from the past year papers By~Kaan Özhan.pdf","page":10,"group":"science","major":"Science & Tech","era":"Early modern","stem":"In the triad attributed to Vitruvius, which term refers to structural firmness?","choices":["firmitas","venustas","utilitas","decorum","proportio"],"answer":"firmitas","explanation":"Firmitas means firmness, one of Vitruvius’s three architectural qualities.","work":"Vitruvian design: stability","artist":"firmitas","priority":5,"proof":"firmitas","format":"single_choice","kind":"source_pdf_context","sourceType":"reviewed_pdf"},{"id":"PDF34-CON-003-A","nodeId":"PDF34-CONFACT-003","source":"Important people from the past year papers By~Kaan Özhan.pdf","page":11,"group":"science","major":"Science & Tech","era":"Early modern","stem":"The astronomical system described in Ptolemy's Almagest placed which body at the centre?","choices":["Earth","Sun","Moon","Jupiter","Mars"],"answer":"Earth","explanation":"Ptolemy’s geocentric model placed Earth at the centre.","work":"Ptolemy's cosmic model","artist":"Earth","priority":5,"proof":"geocentric theory","format":"single_choice","kind":"source_pdf_context","sourceType":"reviewed_pdf"},{"id":"PDF34-CON-004-A","nodeId":"PDF34-CONFACT-004","source":"Important people from the past year papers By~Kaan Özhan.pdf","page":12,"group":"science","major":"Science & Tech","era":"Early modern","stem":"In which year was Newton's Principia published?","choices":["1687","1543","1609","1735","1789"],"answer":"1687","explanation":"Newton published Principia in 1687.","work":"Publication of Newton's Principia","artist":"1687","priority":4,"proof":"1687","format":"single_choice","kind":"source_pdf_context","sourceType":"reviewed_pdf"},{"id":"PDF34-CON-005-A","nodeId":"PDF34-CONFACT-005","source":"Important people from the past year papers By~Kaan Özhan.pdf","page":13,"group":"science","major":"Science & Tech","era":"Early modern","stem":"Which mechanism is most closely associated with Darwin's theory of evolution?","choices":["Natural selection","Spontaneous generation","Inheritance of acquired traits","Geocentrism","Continental drift"],"answer":"Natural selection","explanation":"Darwin explained evolution by natural selection.","work":"Darwin's evolutionary mechanism","artist":"Natural selection","priority":5,"proof":"natural selection","format":"single_choice","kind":"source_pdf_context","sourceType":"reviewed_pdf"},{"id":"PDF34-CON-006-A","nodeId":"PDF34-CONFACT-006","source":"Important people from the past year papers By~Kaan Özhan.pdf","page":16,"group":"writer","major":"Language & Literature","era":"Modern","stem":"Which writer used the pen name George Eliot?","choices":["Mary Ann Evans","Charlotte Brontë","Mary Shelley","Jane Austen","George Sand"],"answer":"Mary Ann Evans","explanation":"George Eliot was the pen name of Mary Ann Evans.","work":"George Eliot's real name","artist":"Mary Ann Evans","priority":4,"proof":"Mary Ann Evans","format":"single_choice","kind":"source_pdf_context","sourceType":"reviewed_pdf"},{"id":"PDF34-CON-007-A","nodeId":"PDF34-CONFACT-007","source":"Important people from the past year papers By~Kaan Özhan.pdf","page":17,"group":"writer","major":"Language & Literature","era":"Modern","stem":"Which name belongs to the author known as Lewis Carroll?","choices":["Charles Lutwidge Dodgson","Charles Dickens","Arthur Conan Doyle","John Ruskin","Thomas Hardy"],"answer":"Charles Lutwidge Dodgson","explanation":"Lewis Carroll was Charles Lutwidge Dodgson’s pen name.","work":"Lewis Carroll's real name","artist":"Charles Lutwidge Dodgson","priority":4,"proof":"Charles Lutwidge Dodgson","format":"single_choice","kind":"source_pdf_context","sourceType":"reviewed_pdf"},{"id":"PDF34-CON-008-A","nodeId":"PDF34-CONFACT-008","source":"Important people from the past year papers By~Kaan Özhan.pdf","page":27,"group":"music","major":"Art History","era":"Modern","stem":"Which term denotes a recurring musical idea often associated with Wagner's operas?","choices":["Leitmotif","Sfumato","Counterpoint","Bel canto","Cantus firmus"],"answer":"Leitmotif","explanation":"A leitmotif is a recurring musical idea linked to a character, idea or situation.","work":"Wagner's recurring musical theme","artist":"Leitmotif","priority":4,"proof":"leitmotif","format":"single_choice","kind":"source_pdf_context","sourceType":"reviewed_pdf"},{"id":"PDF34-CON-009-A","nodeId":"PDF34-CONFACT-009","source":"Important people from the past year papers By~Kaan Özhan.pdf","page":38,"group":"history","major":"History & Politics","era":"Historical","stem":"The empire of Alexander the Great helped spread which culture across the eastern Mediterranean and beyond?","choices":["Hellenistic culture","Carolingian culture","Baroque culture","Byzantine iconoclasm","Industrial culture"],"answer":"Hellenistic culture","explanation":"Alexander’s conquests spread Greek culture and helped form the Hellenistic world.","work":"Hellenistic culture after Alexander","artist":"Hellenistic culture","priority":5,"proof":"Hellenistic","format":"single_choice","kind":"source_pdf_context","sourceType":"reviewed_pdf"},{"id":"PDF34-CON-010-A","nodeId":"PDF34-CONFACT-010","source":"Important people from the past year papers By~Kaan Özhan.pdf","page":39,"group":"history","major":"History & Politics","era":"Historical","stem":"Which religion gained imperial favour after Constantine's conversion?","choices":["Christianity","Buddhism","Zoroastrianism","Judaism","Islam"],"answer":"Christianity","explanation":"Constantine’s conversion and policies raised Christianity’s status in the Roman Empire.","work":"Constantine's change in Roman religious policy","artist":"Christianity","priority":5,"proof":"Christianity","format":"single_choice","kind":"source_pdf_context","sourceType":"reviewed_pdf"},{"id":"PDF34-CON-011-A","nodeId":"PDF34-CONFACT-011","source":"Important people from the past year papers By~Kaan Özhan.pdf","page":41,"group":"history","major":"History & Politics","era":"Historical","stem":"Trajan's Column commemorates Rome's wars against which people?","choices":["Dacians","Carthaginians","Gauls","Persians","Visigoths"],"answer":"Dacians","explanation":"Trajan’s Column commemorates his wars against the Dacians.","work":"Trajan's Column","artist":"Dacians","priority":5,"proof":"Dacian Wars","format":"single_choice","kind":"source_pdf_context","sourceType":"reviewed_pdf"},{"id":"PDF34-CON-012-A","nodeId":"PDF34-CONFACT-012","source":"Important people from the past year papers By~Kaan Özhan.pdf","page":45,"group":"history","major":"History & Politics","era":"Historical","stem":"In which year did Charlemagne become emperor?","choices":["800","476","732","962","1054"],"answer":"800","explanation":"Charlemagne held the imperial title from the year 800.","work":"Charlemagne's imperial accession","artist":"800","priority":5,"proof":"from 800","format":"single_choice","kind":"source_pdf_context","sourceType":"reviewed_pdf"},{"id":"PDF34-CON-013-A","nodeId":"PDF34-CONFACT-013","source":"Important people from the past year papers By~Kaan Özhan.pdf","page":56,"group":"history","major":"History & Politics","era":"Historical","stem":"In which year did Mazzini found Young Italy?","choices":["1831","1789","1815","1848","1861"],"answer":"1831","explanation":"Mazzini founded Young Italy in Marseille in 1831. The source-derived 1832 date has been corrected.","work":"Young Italy founding","artist":"1831","priority":4,"proof":"Young Italy founded in Marseille in 1831; corrected against historical reference.","format":"single_choice","kind":"source_pdf_context","sourceType":"reviewed_pdf","originalProof83":"Young Italy (1832)","references":[{"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Young_Italy","file":"Historical correction to source-derived date"}],"correction83":true},{"id":"PDF34-CON-014-A","nodeId":"PDF34-CONFACT-014","source":"Important people from the past year papers By~Kaan Özhan.pdf","page":58,"group":"history","major":"History & Politics","era":"Historical","stem":"Risorgimento refers to the nineteenth-century movement for the unification of which country?","choices":["Italy","Germany","France","Spain","Greece"],"answer":"Italy","explanation":"The Risorgimento was the movement toward Italian unification.","work":"Meaning of Risorgimento","artist":"Italy","priority":5,"proof":"Italian unification","format":"single_choice","kind":"source_pdf_context","sourceType":"reviewed_pdf"},{"id":"PDF34-CON-015-A","nodeId":"PDF34-CONFACT-015","source":"Important people from the past year papers By~Kaan Özhan.pdf","page":61,"group":"history","major":"History & Politics","era":"Historical","stem":"Which diplomatic meeting was organized by Klemens von Metternich in 1814–15?","choices":["Congress of Vienna","Congress of Berlin","Treaty of Versailles","Peace of Westphalia","Congress of Paris"],"answer":"Congress of Vienna","explanation":"Metternich organized the Congress of Vienna in 1814–15.","work":"Metternich at Vienna","artist":"Congress of Vienna","priority":5,"proof":"Congress of Vienna","format":"single_choice","kind":"source_pdf_context","sourceType":"reviewed_pdf"},{"id":"PDF34-CON-016-A","nodeId":"PDF34-CONFACT-016","source":"Important people from the past year papers By~Kaan Özhan.pdf","page":78,"group":"art-medieval","major":"Art History","era":"Medieval","stem":"In which Italian city is Ambrogio Lorenzetti's Allegory of Good and Bad Government?","choices":["Siena","Florence","Venice","Rome","Padua"],"answer":"Siena","explanation":"The Allegory frescoes are in Siena’s Palazzo Pubblico.","work":"Ambrogio Lorenzetti's civic frescoes","artist":"Siena","priority":5,"proof":"Palazzo Pubblico, Siena","format":"single_choice","kind":"source_pdf_context","sourceType":"reviewed_pdf"},{"id":"PDF34-CON-017-A","nodeId":"PDF34-CONFACT-017","source":"Important people from the past year papers By~Kaan Özhan.pdf","page":91,"group":"art-renaissance","major":"Art History","era":"Renaissance","stem":"Titian's Assumption of the Virgin was made for the high altar of which Venetian church?","choices":["Santa Maria Gloriosa dei Frari","San Marco","Santa Maria della Salute","San Giorgio Maggiore","Santa Maria dei Miracoli"],"answer":"Santa Maria Gloriosa dei Frari","explanation":"Titian painted the altarpiece for the Frari church in Venice.","work":"Titian's Assumption of the Virgin","artist":"Santa Maria Gloriosa dei Frari","priority":4,"proof":"Santa Maria Gloriosa dei","format":"single_choice","kind":"source_pdf_context","sourceType":"reviewed_pdf"},{"id":"PDF34-CON-018-A","nodeId":"PDF34-CONFACT-018","source":"Important people from the past year papers By~Kaan Özhan.pdf","page":98,"group":"art-renaissance","major":"Art History","era":"Renaissance","stem":"Which city houses Veronese's The Feast in the House of Levi in the Gallerie dell'Accademia?","choices":["Venice","Florence","Madrid","Rome","Milan"],"answer":"Venice","explanation":"The painting is in Venice’s Gallerie dell’Accademia.","work":"Veronese's Feast in the House of Levi","artist":"Venice","priority":4,"proof":"Venice","format":"single_choice","kind":"source_pdf_context","sourceType":"reviewed_pdf"},{"id":"PDF34-CON-019-A","nodeId":"PDF34-CONFACT-019","source":"Important people from the past year papers By~Kaan Özhan.pdf","page":104,"group":"art-baroque","major":"Art History","era":"Early modern","stem":"Which museum in Madrid holds Velázquez's Las Meninas?","choices":["Museo del Prado","Museo Reina Sofía","Museo Thyssen-Bornemisza","Museo Cerralbo","Museo Sorolla"],"answer":"Museo del Prado","explanation":"Velázquez’s Las Meninas is held by the Museo del Prado in Madrid.","work":"Where Las Meninas is held","artist":"Museo del Prado","priority":5,"proof":"Museo del Prado","format":"single_choice","kind":"source_pdf_context","sourceType":"reviewed_pdf"},{"id":"PDF34-CON-020-A","nodeId":"PDF34-CONFACT-020","source":"Important people from the past year papers By~Kaan Özhan.pdf","page":108,"group":"art-baroque","major":"Art History","era":"Early modern","stem":"Saturn Devouring His Son belongs to which group of works by Francisco Goya?","choices":["Black Paintings","Caprichos","Disasters of War","Los Proverbios","Portraits of the Royal Family"],"answer":"Black Paintings","explanation":"Goya painted it as part of the Black Paintings.","work":"Goya's Saturn Devouring His Son","artist":"Black Paintings","priority":5,"proof":"Black Paintings","format":"single_choice","kind":"source_pdf_context","sourceType":"reviewed_pdf"},{"id":"PDF34-CON-021-A","nodeId":"PDF34-CONFACT-021","source":"Important people from the past year papers By~Kaan Özhan.pdf","page":114,"group":"art-modern","major":"Art History","era":"20th century","stem":"Which New York museum holds Marc Chagall's I and the Village?","choices":["Museum of Modern Art","Metropolitan Museum of Art","Solomon R. Guggenheim Museum","Whitney Museum of American Art","Frick Collection"],"answer":"Museum of Modern Art","explanation":"I and the Village is held by New York’s Museum of Modern Art.","work":"Chagall's I and the Village","artist":"Museum of Modern Art","priority":3,"proof":"Museum of Modern Art","format":"single_choice","kind":"source_pdf_context","sourceType":"reviewed_pdf"},{"id":"PDF34-CON-022-A","nodeId":"PDF34-CONFACT-022","source":"Important people from the past year papers By~Kaan Özhan.pdf","page":132,"group":"art-modern","major":"Art History","era":"20th century","stem":"Which visual structure is characteristic of Mark Rothko's mature colour-field paintings?","choices":["Irregular rectangular fields of colour","Pointillist dots on a white ground","Perspective grids showing buildings","Readymade found objects","Hard-edged black-and-white stripes"],"answer":"Irregular rectangular fields of colour","explanation":"Rothko’s mature paintings use soft edged, rectangular areas of colour.","work":"Rothko's colour-field style","artist":"Irregular rectangular fields of colour","priority":4,"proof":"rectangular regions of color","format":"single_choice","kind":"source_pdf_context","sourceType":"reviewed_pdf"},{"id":"PDF34-CON-023-A","nodeId":"PDF34-CONFACT-023","source":"Important people from the past year papers By~Kaan Özhan.pdf","page":133,"group":"art-modern","major":"Art History","era":"20th century","stem":"How did Jackson Pollock often position the support while applying poured or splashed paint?","choices":["Horizontally on the floor","Vertically on an easel","Against a curved wall","Inside a glass frame","Under a printing press"],"answer":"Horizontally on the floor","explanation":"Pollock poured and splashed paint onto a horizontal support.","work":"Pollock's drip technique","artist":"Horizontally on the floor","priority":4,"proof":"horizontal surface","format":"single_choice","kind":"source_pdf_context","sourceType":"reviewed_pdf"},{"id":"PDF34-CON-024-A","nodeId":"PDF34-CONFACT-024","source":"Important people from the past year papers By~Kaan Özhan.pdf","page":140,"group":"sculpture-ancient","major":"Art History","era":"Ancient","stem":"The Statue of Zeus at Olympia was counted among which historical group?","choices":["Seven Wonders of the Ancient World","Four Great Basilicas of Rome","Seven Hills of Rome","Seven Liberal Arts","Twelve Labours of Heracles"],"answer":"Seven Wonders of the Ancient World","explanation":"The colossal statue was one of the Seven Wonders of the Ancient World.","work":"Zeus at Olympia and the ancient wonders","artist":"Seven Wonders of the Ancient World","priority":5,"proof":"Seven Wonders","format":"single_choice","kind":"source_pdf_context","sourceType":"reviewed_pdf"},{"id":"PDF34-CON-025-A","nodeId":"PDF34-CONFACT-025","source":"Important people from the past year papers By~Kaan Özhan.pdf","page":143,"group":"sculpture-ancient","major":"Art History","era":"Ancient","stem":"The Canon associated with Polykleitos chiefly concerns ideal proportions of what?","choices":["Human body","Greek temple plan","Roman road network","City walls","Musical instruments"],"answer":"Human body","explanation":"His Canon set out an ideal system of human body proportions.","work":"Polykleitos's Canon","artist":"Human body","priority":5,"proof":"body proportions","format":"single_choice","kind":"source_pdf_context","sourceType":"reviewed_pdf"},{"id":"PDF34-CON-026-A","nodeId":"PDF34-CONFACT-026","source":"Important people from the past year papers By~Kaan Özhan.pdf","page":154,"group":"sculpture-modern","major":"Art History","era":"Modern","stem":"The Three Graces by Antonio Canova belongs chiefly to which artistic movement?","choices":["Neoclassicism","Rococo","Cubism","Art Nouveau","Expressionism"],"answer":"Neoclassicism","explanation":"Canova’s marble group is a major work of Neoclassical sculpture.","work":"Canova's Three Graces","artist":"Neoclassicism","priority":4,"proof":"neoclassical","format":"single_choice","kind":"source_pdf_context","sourceType":"reviewed_pdf"},{"id":"PDF34-CON-027-A","nodeId":"PDF34-CONFACT-027","source":"Important people from the past year papers By~Kaan Özhan.pdf","page":156,"group":"sculpture-modern","major":"Art History","era":"Modern","stem":"Which Naples chapel houses Giuseppe Sanmartino's Veiled Christ?","choices":["Cappella Sansevero","Sistine Chapel","Scrovegni Chapel","Brancacci Chapel","Palatine Chapel"],"answer":"Cappella Sansevero","explanation":"The Veiled Christ is in Naples’s Cappella Sansevero.","work":"Sanmartino's Veiled Christ","artist":"Cappella Sansevero","priority":5,"proof":"Cappella Sansevero","format":"single_choice","kind":"source_pdf_context","sourceType":"reviewed_pdf"},{"id":"PDF34-CON-028-A","nodeId":"PDF34-CONFACT-028","source":"Important people from the past year papers By~Kaan Özhan.pdf","page":164,"group":"sculpture-renaissance","major":"Art History","era":"Renaissance","stem":"Which material was used for Michelangelo's David of 1501–1504?","choices":["Marble","Bronze","Limestone","Terracotta","Plaster"],"answer":"Marble","explanation":"Michelangelo carved the David of 1501–1504 in marble.","work":"Michelangelo's David material","artist":"Marble","priority":5,"proof":"marble","format":"single_choice","kind":"source_pdf_context","sourceType":"reviewed_pdf"},{"id":"PDF34-CON-029-A","nodeId":"PDF34-CONFACT-029","source":"Important people from the past year papers By~Kaan Özhan.pdf","page":175,"group":"architecture-renaissance","major":"Architecture","era":"Renaissance","stem":"Which painter decorated Andrea Palladio's Villa Barbaro with frescoes?","choices":["Paolo Veronese","Tintoretto","Titian","Giotto","Caravaggio"],"answer":"Paolo Veronese","explanation":"Palladio designed the villa; Paolo Veronese painted its frescoes.","work":"Villa Barbaro collaborators","artist":"Paolo Veronese","priority":5,"proof":"Paolo Veronese","format":"single_choice","kind":"source_pdf_context","sourceType":"reviewed_pdf"},{"id":"PDF34-CON-030-A","nodeId":"PDF34-CONFACT-030","source":"Important people from the past year papers By~Kaan Özhan.pdf","page":177,"group":"architecture-renaissance","major":"Architecture","era":"Renaissance","stem":"Who designed the perspective stage scenery of Palladio's Teatro Olimpico?","choices":["Vincenzo Scamozzi","Donato Bramante","Filippo Brunelleschi","Gian Lorenzo Bernini","Andrea Palladio"],"answer":"Vincenzo Scamozzi","explanation":"Vincenzo Scamozzi designed the perspective stage scenery after Palladio’s design.","work":"Teatro Olimpico stage scenery","artist":"Vincenzo Scamozzi","priority":4,"proof":"Vincenzo Scamozzi","format":"single_choice","kind":"source_pdf_context","sourceType":"reviewed_pdf"},{"id":"PDF34-CON-031-A","nodeId":"PDF34-CONFACT-031","source":"Important people from the past year papers By~Kaan Özhan.pdf","page":179,"group":"architecture-renaissance","major":"Architecture","era":"Renaissance","stem":"Bramante's Tempietto at San Pietro in Montorio marks a traditional site associated with the crucifixion of whom?","choices":["Saint Peter","Saint Paul","Saint Mark","Saint John","Saint Andrew"],"answer":"Saint Peter","explanation":"The Tempietto marks the traditional location of Saint Peter’s crucifixion.","work":"Tempietto's commemorated location","artist":"Saint Peter","priority":4,"proof":"St. Peter's crucifixion","format":"single_choice","kind":"source_pdf_context","sourceType":"reviewed_pdf"},{"id":"PDF34-CON-032-A","nodeId":"PDF34-CONFACT-032","source":"Important people from the past year papers By~Kaan Özhan.pdf","page":205,"group":"architecture-modern","major":"Architecture","era":"20th century","stem":"Near which French town is Le Corbusier's Villa Savoye located?","choices":["Poissy","Versailles","Lyon","Chartres","Avignon"],"answer":"Poissy","explanation":"Villa Savoye stands near Poissy, outside Paris.","work":"Villa Savoye's location","artist":"Poissy","priority":4,"proof":"Poissy","format":"single_choice","kind":"source_pdf_context","sourceType":"reviewed_pdf"},{"id":"PDF34-CON-033-A","nodeId":"PDF34-CONFACT-033","source":"Important people from the past year papers By~Kaan Özhan.pdf","page":206,"group":"architecture-modern","major":"Architecture","era":"20th century","stem":"What was Le Corbusier's Ville Radieuse?","choices":["An unrealised urban design proposal","A completed residential tower","A railway station in Paris","A medieval walled city","A Baroque royal palace"],"answer":"An unrealised urban design proposal","explanation":"Le Corbusier’s Ville Radieuse was an unbuilt urban design proposal.","work":"Ville Radieuse status","artist":"An unrealised urban design proposal","priority":4,"proof":"unrealised","format":"single_choice","kind":"source_pdf_context","sourceType":"reviewed_pdf"},{"id":"PDF34-CON-034-A","nodeId":"PDF34-CONFACT-034","source":"Important people from the past year papers By~Kaan Özhan.pdf","page":212,"group":"architecture-modern","major":"Architecture","era":"20th century","stem":"Frank Lloyd Wright's Robie House is associated with which architectural style?","choices":["Prairie style","International Style","Brutalism","Baroque","Deconstructivism"],"answer":"Prairie style","explanation":"Frank Lloyd Wright’s Robie House is a Prairie style building.","work":"Robie House architectural style","artist":"Prairie style","priority":5,"proof":"Prairie style","format":"single_choice","kind":"source_pdf_context","sourceType":"reviewed_pdf"},{"id":"PDF34-CON-035-A","nodeId":"PDF34-CONFACT-035","source":"Important people from the past year papers By~Kaan Özhan.pdf","page":218,"group":"architecture-modern","major":"Architecture","era":"20th century","stem":"The Seagram Building in New York is noted for a facade incorporating which metal?","choices":["Bronze","Copper","Gold","Lead","Titanium"],"answer":"Bronze","explanation":"The Seagram Building is noted for its bronze facade components.","work":"Seagram Building facade material","artist":"Bronze","priority":4,"proof":"bronze","format":"single_choice","kind":"source_pdf_context","sourceType":"reviewed_pdf"},{"id":"PDF34-CON-036-A","nodeId":"PDF34-CONFACT-036","source":"Important people from the past year papers By~Kaan Özhan.pdf","page":224,"group":"architecture-modern","major":"Architecture","era":"20th century","stem":"In which city stands the Dancing House designed by Milunić and Gehry?","choices":["Prague","Vienna","Berlin","Bilbao","Budapest"],"answer":"Prague","explanation":"The Dancing House is in Prague, Czech Republic.","work":"Dancing House's city","artist":"Prague","priority":4,"proof":"Prague","format":"single_choice","kind":"source_pdf_context","sourceType":"reviewed_pdf"}]